Matplotlib Important Functions --- Quick Notes

1. Import Matplotlib

import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

2. Basic Plot

plt.plot(x, y)

Creates a line plot.

3. Line Plot with Formatting

plt.plot(x, y, color="blue", linewidth=2, linestyle="--",
         marker="o", markersize=6)

Common options: - color --- line color - linewidth --- line
thickness - linestyle --- -, --, :, -. - marker --- o,
s, ^, *, x - markersize --- marker size

4. Scatter Plot

plt.scatter(x, y)

Useful for showing relationships between two variables.

Example:

plt.scatter(x, y, color="red", marker="o")

5. Bar Chart

plt.bar(categories, values)

Horizontal bar:

plt.barh(categories, values)

6. Histogram

plt.hist(data, bins=10)

Used to show the distribution of numerical data.

Useful options:

plt.hist(data, bins=10, edgecolor="black", alpha=0.7)

7. Pie Chart

plt.pie(values, labels=labels, autopct="%1.1f%%")

Example:

plt.pie(values, labels=labels, autopct="%1.1f%%",
        startangle=90)

8. Labels

plt.xlabel("X Axis")
plt.ylabel("Y Axis")

9. Title

plt.title("My Chart")

Formatting:

plt.title("My Chart", fontsize=16, color="blue")

10. Legend

plt.legend()

With labels:

plt.plot(x, y, label="Training Loss")
plt.legend()

11. Grid

plt.grid(True)

Formatted grid:

plt.grid(True, linestyle="--", alpha=0.5)

12. X and Y Axis Limits

plt.xlim(0, 10)
plt.ylim(0, 100)

13. Ticks

plt.xticks([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])
plt.yticks([0, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100])

Rotate x-axis labels:

plt.xticks(rotation=45)

14. Figure Size

plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))

15. Multiple Lines

plt.plot(x, y1, label="Model 1")
plt.plot(x, y2, label="Model 2")
plt.legend()

16. Multiple Subplots

plt.subplot(2, 1, 1)
plt.plot(x, y)

plt.subplot(2, 1, 2)
plt.bar(x, y)

Recommended modern approach:

fig, ax = plt.subplots(2, 1)
ax[0].plot(x, y)
ax[1].bar(x, y)

17. Add Text

plt.text(x, y, "Important Point")

18. Add Annotation

plt.annotate("Maximum", xy=(x, y))

19. Vertical and Horizontal Lines

plt.axvline(x=5, linestyle="--")
plt.axhline(y=10, linestyle="--")

20. Fill Area

plt.fill_between(x, y, alpha=0.3)

21. Set Axis Labels Together

plt.xlabel("Epoch")
plt.ylabel("Loss")

22. Save a Figure

plt.savefig("chart.png")

High-quality image:

plt.savefig("chart.png", dpi=300, bbox_inches="tight")

23. Display the Figure

plt.show()

24. Clear the Current Figure

plt.clf()

25. Close a Figure

plt.close()

